> planner/feedback.py
> """
> Feedback event capture and response-to-plan attribution.
> 
> Feedback is always linked to immutable response records, not a mutable current
> responder. Thumbs are useful satisfaction signals, but they are not equivalent
> to truthfulness, source quality, or reliability.
> 
> Public API:
> 
> class FeedbackService:
>     def vote_up(self, response_id: str) -> FeedbackEvent: ...
>     def vote_down(self, response_id: str) -> FeedbackEvent: ...
> 
>     def feedback(
>         self,
>         response_id: str,
>         *,
>         kind: Literal["thumb_up", "thumb_down", "correction", "rating", "edit"],
>         value: Any = None,
>     ) -> FeedbackEvent: ...
> 
> Caller:
> - planner.py exposes `vote_up`, `vote_down`, and eventually `feedback`.
> - FeedbackService reads the ResponseRecord from persistence.py.
> - It writes durable feedback events and forwards attributable learning signals
>   to evaluation.py / selection.py.
> """
> 
> =====
> planner/evaluation.py
> """
> Quality, reliability, and offline evaluation.
> 
> This module prevents chat thumbs from becoming the sole optimization target.
> It maintains separate evidence for satisfaction, task quality, factuality,
> source grounding, calibration, policy compliance, tests, and failures.
> 
> Public API:
> 
> class Evaluator(Protocol):
>     def evaluate(
>         self,
>         record: ResponseRecord,
>         response: Response | None,
>         context: PlannerContext,
>     ) -> EvaluationResult: ...
> 
> class EvaluationService:
>     def record_feedback(self, feedback: FeedbackEvent) -> None: ...
>     def record_evaluation(self, result: EvaluationResult) -> None: ...
>     def update_plan_evidence(self, plan: PlanSpec) -> None: ...
>     def run_offline_suite(self, suite: EvaluationSuite) -> list[EvaluationResult]: ...
> 
> Evaluation suites should cover representative real work: research, coding,
> technical/numerical analysis, project continuity, planning, writing, and
> source-grounded factual tasks. Prefer objective tests when possible.
> 
> Caller:
> - feedback.py forwards user feedback.
> - workflow may schedule verification evaluators.
> - selection.py consumes summarized evidence, never raw evaluator internals.
> """
> 
